body:
### Tested versions

- Reproducible in 4.6.stable
- Reproducible in 4.7.dev2
- Reproducible in 4.0.stable


### System information

Godot v4.6.stable - macOS Tahoe (26.3.1) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Metal (Forward+) - integrated Apple M3 Pro (Apple9) - Apple M3 Pro (11 threads) - 18.00 GiB memory

### Issue description

When sampling a GradientTexture1D using the following shader:

```	
shader_type spatial;

uniform sampler2D ramp_texture;

void vertex() {
	// Called for every vertex the material is visible on.
}

void fragment() {
	ALBEDO = texture(ramp_texture, vec2(0.0,0)).rgb;
	// Called for every pixel the material is visible on.
}

//void light() {
//	// Called for every pixel for every light affecting the material.
//	// Uncomment to replace the default light processing function with this one.
//}
```

I get the color that is _actually_ at UV 1.0

e.g. with a ramp that goes from black @ 0.0 to white @ 1.0,  when inputting 0.0 as the UV into texture(), the colour returned is white, not black as it should be.

### Steps to reproduce

1. Start w/ a blank project
2. Add a MeshInstance node
3. Set it up w/ a quad mesh
4. Set the override material to a new shader material
5. Set this as the shader code:
``` 
shader_type spatial;

uniform sampler2D ramp_texture;

void vertex() {
	// Called for every vertex the material is visible on.
}

void fragment() {
	ALBEDO = texture(ramp_texture, vec2(0.0,0)).rgb;
	// Called for every pixel the material is visible on.
}

//void light() {
//	// Called for every pixel for every light affecting the material.
//	// Uncomment to replace the default light processing function with this one.
//}

```
7. Add the default ramp texture to the sampler2d in the shader parameters section.
8. et voila, a white quad that should be black.
9. Note that if you nudge the UV to 0.001, it outputs black as it ought to.

### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)

[color-ramp-bug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/26102347/color-ramp-bug.zip)
